WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.290
An infirmary in Edinburgh.

2
00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:03.900
An iron bed.

3
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:05.990
A crutch against the wall.

4
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.300
The patient, W.

5
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:07.500
E.

6
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:10.400
Henley, lost a leg as a teenager.

7
00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:13.340
A surgeon is fighting
to save the other one.

8
00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:15.390
Here, he writes a poem.

9
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:20.220
It begins: "Out of the night that
covers me," And near the end:

10
00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:24.590
"I am the master of my fate:"
He can't control his body.

11
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.510
So how can he claim that?

12
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:32.740
In this mission, you'll find out how the poem
got its Latin title, Invictus: unconquered.

13
00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.850
You'll feel its steady
beat: four stresses,

14
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.520
line after line.

15
00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.580
And you'll weigh what happens to him.

16
00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:42.290
Is anything left he can still control?

17
00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.840
Your mission: explain how he can
call himself master of his fate.
